    "en": {
      "shared_perspectives": "German media across the political spectrum agree that the Ukraine war has forced a decisive shift in Germany’s security strategy, prompting a broadly shared call for the Bundeswehr to meet NATO’s 2 percent spending target and to undergo deep structural reforms, especially in digital and cyber capabilities. At the same time, there is a common recognition that the traditional conscription model is increasingly seen as outdated, with both right‑leaning and left‑leaning outlets reporting growing public pressure to replace it with a professional volunteer force. Finally, despite divergent views on specific deployments, most outlets converge on the view that Germany must assume a more reliable role within NATO, balancing heightened defense commitments with heightened scrutiny of arms exports and overseas missions.",
